    2. Series - A series is like a row or a column

> Whenever we are working with Pandas, we need to first load the data.
  More conveniently, we can work with excel spreadsheet or .csv(comma separated values) file

> Pandas are good at representing two dimensional data. So, where you have some rows and columns.

> Loading a DataFrame;

df = pd.read_csv('data.csv')        # Load from CSV
df = pd.read_excel('data.xlsx')     # Load from Excel
df = pd.DataFrame(data_dict)        # Load from dictionary

> To manually create a dataframe using dictionary;

import pandas as pd

data = {
    'Name': ['Alice', 'Bob', 'Charlie'],
    'Age': [25, 30, 35],
    'Country': ['USA', 'Canada', 'UK']
}

df = pd.DataFrame(data)
print(df)

